# arena_set_sharer

## Product

Cloud auth and document share for **arena_set_cracker**. The client owns discovery, Scryfall, Arena parse, and the local vault. This server holds accounts, user documents, and (when there is multi-user data) community-aggregated insight such as pairing rates.

A formal demo is a signed-in document surface.

## Stack map

- Kotlin / Spring Boot 3.5, package `com.example.arena_set_sharer`
- Postgres via Docker Compose; Liquibase at `src/main/resources/liquibase/changelog.xml`
- JPA for `users` and `password_resets`; user documents are JSONB when that table exists
- JWT + BCrypt + HMAC email; SES for reset mail
- `bootRun` loads gitignored `.env` (see `.env.example`). Tests use `src/test/resources/application.properties`

## Where the brain lives

| Concern | Owner |
|---------|--------|
| Login / register / JWT | `AuthenticationRestController`, `UserService`, `JwtUtil` |
| Password reset | `PasswordResetService`, `AwsSesMailService` |
| Authn boundary | `SecurityConfig`, `JwtRequestFilter` |
| User documents / ingest | `DocumentRestController`, `DocumentService` |
| Schema | `liquibase/changelog.xml` |

## Commits

Ask where the user is before committing. First line: `<place> <goal>` (Hideaway is a place-stamp, not a magic title and not assumed).

Body only when the goal needs grains above the diff. Prefer verb-led, natural bullets. Signpost with **one fixed name** per surface (class, table, owner)—do not invent aliases for the same thing. Prefer a short domain phrase over listing every new symbol when that domain owns them. When the same commit includes a preliminary that enables the goal, list that bullet first. Track files (or their owners) nested under the domain change. Header-only when the diff is one file and obvious. Do not restate the header, the product story, or work that is not in the diff.

Fold same-story follow-ups into the unpushed commit. Leave unrelated fixes as their own commit. Do not rewrite anything already on the remote.

Only commit when the user asks.

## Comments

Comments record durable why that the code does not show. Put session teaching and “not X” rebuttals in the chat. Do not narrate a choice the identifiers already name.

```kotlin
// BAD — play-by-play the next reader gets from the bindings
// Hash the email, then store the hash.

// GOOD — why HMAC and not a column of plaintext
// email_hash: HMAC so a dumped users table is not a mailing list.
```

## Tests

`./gradlew test` starts Compose Postgres and runs the context-load smoke. Prefer that over inventing a suite mid-feature.

## Refactors

Propose preliminary or structural cleanups that would enable the task; wait for assent before expanding into them.

## Session scope

Treat document ingest, formal demo, and community pairing as **in or out of scope only when the user says so** for that session.

Read `.cursor/FOLLOWUPS.md` for intentional deferrals. That file is local and not in git.
